WEBVTT

NOTE V2500 HPT Disk Scan Tutorial - Mastercut captions

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
V2500 HPT Disk Scan Tutorial - verified mastercut.

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.500
V2500 HPT Disk - Stage 1.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.000
Immersion scan plan - a full walkthrough.

4
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:15.500
Step 1. Setup the immersion tank.

5
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.500
Mount the disk on the turntable, fill the tank,

6
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:21.500
and position the probe at an 8-inch water path.

7
00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:24.500
Step 2. Open the scan plan.

8
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.500
Select the V2500 Stage 1 preset -

9
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:31.000
five zones populate automatically from procedure NDIP 1226.

10
00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:34.000
Step 3. Anatomy of the disk.

11
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Five inspection zones -

12
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.000
E, the upper web transition.

13
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.500
A, the upper chamfer.

14
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.000
B, the upper land.

15
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.500
C, the bore entry.

16
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:43.300
D, the bore inner diameter.

17
00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.500
Step 4. Zone E plus 45-degree pass.

18
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:50.500
The probe approaches at plus 45 degrees,
the disk rotates 360,

19
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:54.500
and the probe steps radially in two-hundredths-inch increments.

20
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.000
Every position is logged into the C-scan.

21
00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:01.500
Step 5. Zone E minus 45-degree pass.

22
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:05.500
The shear direction changes, and the sweep repeats in the opposite direction

23
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.700
for full bidirectional coverage.

24
00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:11.500
Step 6. Zones A through D.

25
00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:15.500
Each zone is scanned twice, plus and minus 45 degrees -

26
00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:19.500
ten passes in total.

27
00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:22.500
Step 7. Live C-scan capture.

28
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.500
The colormap builds up as the probe moves -

29
00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:30.500
peak amplitude per position, indications above 20% FSH are flagged.

30
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:32.700
Watch the data come in.

31
00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:36.000
Inspection results.

32
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Five C-scan strips, one per zone -

33
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.300
no reportable indications, this disk is clean.

34
00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:46.500
Step 8. Save the scan data.

35
00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:49.900
Enter the part serial number and click Save.

36
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:50.800
Inspection complete.

37
00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:51.150
Five zones, ten passes, zero indications.

38
00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:56.500
Missing chapter: calibration before the bore scan.

39
00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:04.800
Verify FBH reference, DAC or TCG, 80 percent FSH, water path and incidence before scanning.

40
00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:10.800
Missing chapter: Stage 2 is a separate scan plan.

41
00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:19.100
Stage 2 uses P/N 2A4802, NDIP-1227 Rev D and zones M, N, O, P, K, L.

42
00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:25.800
Missing chapter: post-calibration and traceability.

43
00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:31.600
Review by surface, rescan questionable data, document post-cal and save traceable records.

44
00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:37.900
Final rule: the approved current procedure controls production inspection.
